<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kedah Sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1136 CE – present (approx.) · capital Alor Setar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the oldest continuous monarchies in the world, a Malay sultanate that converted to Islam in the 12th century and survives as a state of Malaysia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>According to the Kedah annals, the ruler of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/old-kedah">Old Kedah</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phra-ong-mahawangsa">Phra Ong Mahawangsa</a>, accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> in 1136 and took the name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Mudzaffar Shah, founding a line that continues today. The date is traditional. The sultans later moved their seat to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alor-setar">Alor Setar</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> plains of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kedah-river">Kedah River</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Kedah was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> bowl of the peninsula, exporting grain, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a> and elephants. Its rulers sent the bunga mas, golden flowers, to Siam as a sign of tribute while seeking other allies. In 1786 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdullah-mukarram-shah">Abdullah Mukarram Shah</a> allowed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-light">Francis Light</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">British East India Company</a> to occupy <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prince-of-wales-island">Penang</a>, hoping for protection that never came.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Siam invaded in 1821 and ruled directly until 1842. By the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-siamese-treaty-of-1909">Anglo-Siamese Treaty of 1909</a> Kedah passed to British protection as one of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/unfederated-malay-states">Unfederated Malay States</a>, and it joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federation-of-malaya">Federation of Malaya</a> in 1948. Its royal house still reigns, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunku-abdul-rahman">Tunku Abdul Rahman</a>, Malaysia's first prime minister, was a Kedah prince.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kedah-sultanate.jpg" alt="Kedah Sultanate" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Bukhrin at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Kedah.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1136 CE – present (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Alor Setar</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mudzaffar Shah I, Abdullah Mukarram Shah, Abdul Hamid Halim Shah</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malay</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/malaysia">Malaysia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sultanate of Kedah, Kedah</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1581&amp;focus=kedah-sultanate" aria-label="Kedah Sultanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7460 1949 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kedah Sultanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7780 2205L7783 2219M7780 2205L7752 1900M7780 2205L7754 1922M7780 2205L7823 2316M7780 2205L7776 2191"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7783 2219h0M7752 1900h0M7754 1922h0M7823 2316h0M7776 2191h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7780 2205h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7780 2205h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Alor Setar. <a href="/atlas?year=1581&amp;focus=kedah-sultanate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
